From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Chulo <cchulo.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus-ally: scale rumble and vibration intensity to
 0..100

ally_x_play_effect() converts the 16-bit FF_RUMBLE magnitudes with
"/ 512", which gives 0..127. The 0x0d rumble report is the Xbox
wireless controller rumble block (enable, left trigger, right trigger,
strong, weak, duration, delay, loop count), and its magnitudes are
percentages, 0..100. Every other implementation that writes this
report uses that range:

- InputPlumber v0.83.1, src/drivers/rog_ally/hid_report.rs
  ("Magnitudes range 0-100") and driver.rs (clamps each field to 100),
- hhd, src/hhd/device/rog_ally/base.py, AllyXHidraw.consume()
  (min(100, magnitude * 100)),
- kndclark/ally_module, hid-asus.c, ALLY_FF_MAX_INTENSITY 100,
- hid-microsoft.c, ms_play_effect() (magnitude * 100 / U16_MAX for the
  same block on the Xbox One S controller).

So any request above about 78 % produced an out-of-range value
(101..127). What the MCU does with those values is not documented. On
an RC74XA (ROG Xbox Ally X20) the owner reports that 100 % through the
evdev FF path feels like about 25 %, which fits firmware that wraps or
rejects values above 100.

Scale with DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(magnitude * 100, 0xffff), so 0xffff maps
to 100 and 0x8000 to 50.

gamepad_vibration_intensity_store() rejects values above 64, but the
driver itself initialises both channels to 0x64 (100) and the MCU
command takes 0..100 (hhd's COMMIT_RESET sends 0x64 by default,
ally_module accepts 0..100). Allow 0..100 so userspace can restore the
default.

Derived from: the report layout in InputPlumber v0.83.1
(src/drivers/rog_ally/hid_report.rs, commit dbcd6c06 "feat: Add trigger
haptics for the ROG Ally / Xbox Ally X"), hhd commit eca609b0
(src/hhd/device/rog_ally/base.py, const.py), kndclark/ally_module
commit 3422a5db (hid-asus.c) and drivers/hid/hid-microsoft.c in the same
tree.

Base: linux-integration 7.2.7-valve2 plus the previous patches in this
series.

DRAFT, not built or tested. TODO(hw): on an RC74XA, run
vm/guest/rumble-test.py at 25, 50, 75 and 100 % before and after; 100 %
must now be the strongest level. Check that
"echo 100 100 > gamepad_vibration_intensity" is accepted.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
index 8d46330..4a5638a 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
@@ -29,6 +29,14 @@
 #define FEATURE_ROG_ALLY_REPORT_ID 0x5a
 #define FEATURE_ROG_ALLY_CODE_PAGE 0xD1
 #define FEATURE_ROG_ALLY_REPORT_SIZE 64
+
+/*
+ * Rumble motor magnitudes in the 0x0d report and the MCU vibration
+ * intensity (xpad_cmd_set_vibe_intensity) are percentages, 0..100.
+ */
+#define ALLY_FF_MAX_MAGNITUDE 100
+#define ALLY_VIBE_MAX_INTENSITY 100
+
 #define ALLY_X_INPUT_REPORT_USB 0x0B
 #define ALLY_X_INPUT_REPORT_USB_SIZE 16
 
@@ -425,7 +433,7 @@ struct ally_gamepad_cfg {
 	struct btn_mapping key_mapping[xpad_mode_mouse];
 	/*
 	 * index: left, right
-	 * max: 64
+	 * max: ALLY_VIBE_MAX_INTENSITY (100)
 	 */
 	u8 vibration_intensity[2];
 
@@ -730,7 +738,7 @@ static ssize_t gamepad_vibration_intensity_store(struct device *dev,
 	if (sscanf(buf, "%d %d", &left, &right) != 2)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (left > 64 || right > 64)
+	if (left > ALLY_VIBE_MAX_INTENSITY || right > ALLY_VIBE_MAX_INTENSITY)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	ally_cfg->vibration_intensity[0] = left;
@@ -1659,8 +1667,10 @@ static int ally_x_play_effect(struct input_dev *idev, void *data, struct ff_effe
 		return 0;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ally_x->lock, flags);
-	ally_x->ff_packet->ff.magnitude_strong = effect->u.rumble.strong_magnitude / 512;
-	ally_x->ff_packet->ff.magnitude_weak = effect->u.rumble.weak_magnitude / 512;
+	ally_x->ff_packet->ff.magnitude_strong =
+		DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(effect->u.rumble.strong_magnitude * ALLY_FF_MAX_MAGNITUDE, 0xffff);
+	ally_x->ff_packet->ff.magnitude_weak =
+		DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(effect->u.rumble.weak_magnitude * ALLY_FF_MAX_MAGNITUDE, 0xffff);
 	ally_x->update_ff = true;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ally_x->lock, flags);
 
